Subject: Cantor Temporal Planner and Bidirectional Change Reflection Plan

Description: Dependency plan following CTPR canonical formation. It records the deterministic implementation frontier and later operational adapters without activating them.

@ [plan_uuid] a7abdf6a-73d4-4f9a-94f1-01b86ea986b1
@ [source_snapshot_uuid] a0b27483-1bde-43c6-abd9-23dddc31c51d
@ [plan_status] designed_not_activated

& [Phase_0_CanonicalAuthority] is current
  + bind source, SMTC dependency, exploded, refinement, data, external fidelity, constraints, pruning, exhaustion, justification, registry, requirements, canonical, and phase lock
  + authorize CTPR semantics and proof obligations only
  + stop before runtime implementation

& [Phase_1_PureForms] maps to WS-CTPR-010
  + implement immutable forms for repository generation, task contract refs, plans, time, calendar, events, content, snapshots, capsules, diffs, lanes, messages, returns, joins, compiler generations, invalidation, and lessons
  + implement normalized serialization and pure validation
  + reject unknown fields, invalid identities, illegal states, and unsupported versions
  + permit no clock, filesystem, Git, provider, calendar, database, thread, service, notification, or external effect
  + [activation] valid CTPR signature plus explicit worker claim

& [Phase_2_DeterministicComponents] depends_on Phase_1
  + [WS-CTPR-011] fake logical-time event repository, snapshots, materiality, Calendar, Planner, recurrence, wake revalidation, and replay
  + [WS-CTPR-012] tandem messages, acknowledgments, release barriers, invalidation, timeout, cancellation, and crash reentry
  + [WS-CTPR-013] bounded SMTC source, semantic, build, impact, correspondence, and proof diff fixture
  + components may be developed independently only against the same signed forms

& [Phase_3_IntegratedFirstProof] maps to WS-CTPR-014
  + create a three-step objective with estimates, deadline, review checkpoint, one recurring candidate routine, and one reversible simulated effect
  + preserve the selected plan and deliberately deviate during the middle step
  + append material task, tool, simulated-effect, review, and calendar events
  + rear review detects deviation and new requirement and refuses premature completion
  + ObserverJoin invalidates prepared dependent work, replans, and releases the corrected step
  + compiler fixture performs source, semantic, impact, correspondence, and proof diffs
  + normalized replay reproduces final admitted state
  + negatives reject stale version, unsourced time, unrelated diff, missing reflection, false snapshot, history rewrite, hidden effect, and self-certification

& [Phase_4_ReleaseAudit] maps to WS-CTPR-015
  + reconcile every CTPR requirement with code, test, proof, residual, and authority status
  + run fresh quality and deterministic replay checks
  + record complete, partial, failed, deferred, superseded, or no-benefit outcomes honestly
  + preserve rollback and source lineage

& [Phase_5_OperatorShellHandoff] maps to WS-CTPR-016
  + expose read-only E0/E1 temporal proposals, task history, review status, and reentry only under separate COS authority
  + use fake desktop and local logical-time fixtures first
  + grant no ambient observation, live calendar, notification, desktop, or external effect

& [LaterOperationalProfiles] require new source and SJS
  + live clock and civil-time library
  + calendar provider synchronization
  + notification adapters
  + bounded background material-event capture
  + filesystem and Git projections
  + database or event-store persistence
  + concurrent or distributed lane transport
  + model-backed Planner or rear reviewer
  + ECS runtime projection
  + model-training corpus and pipeline
  + FPGA interpreter or native projection

& [StopAndRerouteConditions] are mandatory
  + source, SMTC, external evidence, canonical, or signature drift
  + inability to represent one requirement without guessed semantics
  + history rewrite, false atomicity, mixed attribution, privacy leak, or unbounded retention
  + stale release, shared mutable state, missing review, deadlock, or nondeterministic replay
  + compiler self-certification or target loss without declaration
  + model or ECS path gives no measured benefit over exact fallback
  + live authority would be required before a separately signed operational profile exists

& [CurrentPlanAuthority] is absent
  + this plan orders future work but does not assign, implement, execute, synchronize, notify, observe in background, mutate Git, invoke a provider, train a model, select ECS, or synthesize hardware
